// A module-private module-level VARIABLE may not be read through `Mod.name`.
//
// This is the read-path twin of visibility_module_private_alias.sf, and the test
// that would have been green against the broken compiler: `Lib.mod_secret_var`
// is a MemberAccess, not a MethodCall, so it bypassed the check_module_ref_visibility
// call in the MethodCall arm entirely. infer_member_access's module-alias branch
// now routes a bare read through the same check. If this file ever compiles clean,
// module-level `private var`/`let` has stopped being enforced again.
import "../support/visibility_module_lib.sf" as Lib

IO.println(Lib.mod_secret_var)
